11.0.0 — one name, Echoelmusic; a stream and a take finish stopping before the next begins

What is new since 10067. Each line is code that the Echoel Studio run builds; only the stream's
four states have tests of their own, and nothing here is device-verified yet.
- Name: the name under the app's icon is Echoelmusic (it was Echoel). The app's messages, the
  About page ("About Echoelmusic"), the purchase page ("Echoelmusic Plugins"), the Siri
  examples on the Learn page ("Play Echoelmusic") and the permission questions iOS asks say
  the same.
- Audio Units in other apps: the 29 units are registered as "Echoelmusic: Synth",
  "Echoelmusic: EQ" and so on. Type, subtype and manufacturer code are unchanged.
- MIDI and lights: the MIDI 2.0 source another app sees is "Echoelmusic MPE (MIDI 2.0)", the
  timecode source "Echoelmusic Timecode", the sACN source name "Echoelmusic" — choose them
  again once where a routing was saved.
- Go Live: Stop Stream closes every destination before Go Live is offered again; the page says
  "Stopping" meanwhile. A destination that answers after Stop no longer brings the stream back.
- Background: with nothing playing the audio stops when the app leaves the screen, as before.
  The app now also counts its input as closed there, so a song that stops needing the input
  while away comes back without the microphone.
- Recording: after a take is stopped, Record is unavailable until the take's file is closed,
  instead of starting a take that had to be thrown away.
- Export Video and Export Field Layer (Alpha): when the mix cannot be rendered — a plugin
  stops, or the song is too long — the export stops and says why, instead of writing a film
  without sound. A film says what its mix was exported without, and a Field layer no longer
  shows a loudness.

Previous: 11.0.0 (10067) — warp modes, a playhead you can move, zoom and waveforms; 10064 — a
de-esser, vocal chains, reverb modes.
Earlier: git history.

Bump this file on a commit whose "Echoel Studio" run is green to upload a build
(.github/workflows/studio-testflight.yml). Build number = 10000 + the workflow's run number.
The version is MARKETING_VERSION in EchoelStudio/project.yml.
This file is a test list for the device, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

Five things to try on the device (answer each yes or no):
1. Home Screen after the update: does the name under the icon read "Echoelmusic" in full, not
   cut off?
2. AUM or GarageBand: are the units listed as "Echoelmusic: Synth", "Echoelmusic: EQ" and so
   on, and does a session saved with the build before still open with its sound?
3. Go Live to a destination, wait for the On Air clock, press Stop Stream, and press Go Live
   again as soon as it is offered: does the page say "Stopping" in between, and does the
   second stream arrive at the destination?
4. Arm an audio track, leave the song stopped, go to the Home Screen for ten seconds and come
   back: does the orange microphone dot go out while you are away, and can you record a take
   at once without arming again?
5. Record an audio take of a minute or more, press Record to end it and Record again at once:
   does a second take start, and are both takes on the track afterwards?
